 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nTIFF image width property returns height value instead\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen working with TIFF images, the `px_width` property is returning the image height value instead of the actual width. This causes incorrect image dimensions to be reported.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx.image.tiff import _TiffParser, _IfdEntries, TIFF_TAG\n\n# Create a TIFF parser with known width and height values\npx_width, px_height = (42, 24)\nentries = {TIFF_TAG.IMAGE_WIDTH: px_width, TIFF_TAG.IMAGE_LENGTH: px_height}\nifd_entries = _IfdEntries(entries)\ntiff_parser = _TiffParser(ifd_entries)\n\nprint(f\"Expected width: {px_width}\")\nprint(f\"Actual width: {tiff_parser.px_width}\")\nprint(f\"Expected height: {px_height}\")\nprint(f\"Actual height: {tiff_parser.px_height}\")\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nExpected width: 42\nActual width: 42\nExpected height: 24\nActual height: 24\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nExpected width: 42\nActual width: 24\nExpected height: 24\nActual height: 24\n```\n\nThe `px_width` property is returning 24 (the height) instead of 42 (the width).\n</issue>\n",
